Apply order 0040 against mariopartyrd/partyboard 98ac07fd1e8f7ab938bbb6fe75789fad99419010 (CC0-1.0; ADR 0009 section 5).
m449dll: pick each racer from its own global, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

M4-07 (E2 game-side proof). Kareening Koopa keeps its two racer objects in (&lbl_1_bss_54)[0] and [1]:
the word at 0x54 and the one after it, which on the console is lbl_1_bss_58 (the decomp names globals by
address, and nothing else uses lbl_1_bss_58). Our compiler lays these globals out in declaration order,
lbl_1_bss_50 after lbl_1_bss_54, so the second racer's store overwrote lbl_1_bss_50, the course object.
The racer setup then read the course's models from a racer (model ids -1) and faulted on a null HSF root
in Hu3DModelObjMtxGet in its first frame.

On MPT_PC every (&lbl_1_bss_54)[i] goes through MPT_M449_RACER(i), which picks lbl_1_bss_54 for 0 and
lbl_1_bss_58 for 1, the console's layout. Code only: no global is added, renamed or resized, because the
state hash names the module's data by symbol (a first version that added an array moved the M1 trail).
Kareening Koopa is reached from Mini-game mode and Story only, never from a party, so no replay or golden
plays this code; state hashes do not move (docs/titles/mp4.md, M1).

